"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Western Front ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "A name used to describe where militaries met in the World Wars.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was part of the Western Front in 1943.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about the past.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "combat", "type": "name"}, {"content": "active fighting", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The stress of combat was overwhelming, so I started smoking. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nasty", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very unpleasant to see, smell, taste, etc.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Smoking is a nasty habit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "port", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a strong, sweet, usually dark red wine that is made in Portugal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I always have a glass of port before bed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to adopt ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take a child of other parents legally as your own child", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I adopted three children.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Writing an Autobiography ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "To write an autobiography you need to follow the next steps:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "1. Write your name and personal information. (date and place of birth) <br> 2. Write about your family life. <br> 3. Write about some of the activities you usually like to do. <br> 4. Write about your most exciting experiences and challenges. <br> 5. Write about things you haven't done that you want to do in the future. <br><br>  <span class=\"strong\">Example:</span><br> <span class=\"italic\">My Autobiography<br> My name is Claire Feeney. I was born in Seattle in 1993. I studied in a nice and quiet school. I live in Seattle with my parents, my siblings and my grandmother. I also have a huge black dog. I love outdoors sports, I usually go hiking to Mount Rainier and sometimes I play baseball with my friends. I also love to travel. I have traveled to Turkey, Peru and Nigeria. I have eaten typical food from all those countries. I haven't visited Colombia yet but I would love to visit my penpal in Bogot\u00e1 some day because I haven't seen her in years.<span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would for Past Habits", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Would</span> and <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> have similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "However, there is an important difference between <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span>. <span class=\"italic\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> does not require this.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I used to smoke a pack of cigarettes a day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I used to eat unhealthy food. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I would often go to bed after midnight.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "You are a reporter for <span class=\"italic\">Cambridge Life</span>.  You have to interview a friend of the family about their life.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask 6-8 questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask about their family, past habits and if they had or haven't had an interesting life.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down their answers in complete sentences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I interview a family member.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask questions about family and past experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write sentences about the life of others.", "type": "text"}]}]}